<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SActionScript version="1" name="mixer_insert_row_menu">

  <!-- MODIFYING A PLUGIN FROM THE MIXER STRIP (QBX-201).

       The mixer mounts the arranger's own insert list in COMPACT mode
       (proposal 48 D5a), where the row's Edit, Reload and Remove buttons are
       hidden. mixer_inserts' header has said since M1 that "nothing becomes
       unreachable, only smaller: Edit is already the row's own double-click,
       and Reload / Remove stay on its context menu" — and the second half of
       that sentence was simply not true. There was no context menu anywhere in
       SPluginEffectStrip, so in the mixer a plugin could not be removed at
       all, and a right-click aimed at one PROPAGATED to SMixerStrip, which
       answered with the TRACK menu: "Remove track" as the first item under a
       gesture meant for a plugin.

       WHAT IS GATED HERE, and the shape of each claim:

       1. The compact row's LAYOUT: the name on its own line one step smaller
          than the row's font, the bypass box a small unlabelled checkmark on
          the line BELOW it, and the Track Detail dock's full row unchanged.
          Read from the LAYOUT and from the fonts, never from geometry — a
          widget built off screen is never mapped, so a rectangle can be true
          of a layout that never ran.

       2. The row's MENU, as the one builder behind the real menu and
          describeRowMenu() reports it: what it offers on an Active row, on a
          Missing one, and which items are greyed.

       3. Every command through the ITEM ITSELF: `plugin-row-command
          gesture="menu"` builds the menu the right-click builds, wires it the
          same way and triggers the named QAction, so the connection from the
          item to SPluginEffectStrip::runRowCommand() is on the path. Both
          REFUSALS are asserted too — Edit and Bypass on a Missing slot, and
          Reload on an Active one — because a verb that reported success there
          would hide the greying, and a greyed item is one a user cannot click
          either.

       4. The DOUBLE-CLICK as a real event delivered to the row's container, so
          the strip's own event filter is what dispatches it. That retires one
          of pluginui/CONTRACT.md's "still manual" items.

       WHAT IS NOT GATED, and cannot be from here: QMenu::exec() itself, the
       event's accept(), and therefore the one claim that follows from the
       accept — that the mixer strip's TRACK menu no longer answers over a
       plugin row. exec() is modal and a headless modal is a hang (no qxa case
       may open one), so the mixer strip's own menu lives with the identical
       limit: proposal 48 AC4.2 gates its three commands through
       runMenuCommand() for exactly this reason. Which row a point is over
       (rowIndexAt) is geometry, and a widget built off screen is never
       mapped. The propagation stays a manual check.

       The row-width claim (`maxRowWidth`) is the measured one. Proposal 48
       found the FULL row's layout minimum at 113 px against a WIDE mixer strip
       of 96, which is why compact mode exists at all; measured again here over
       one row with this fixture's name it is 377 px full and 14 px compact.
       The bound is 60 — SMixerStrip::NARROW_WIDTH, so the compact row fits
       even the narrow column it is hidden in — and the headroom is
       deliberate: a platform whose checkbox indicator is wider must not fail a
       case that is about the stacking. What takes the row from 377 to 14 is
       the name label's size policy: a QLabel's minimum width is its FULL TEXT,
       and a plugin name is longer than a mixer column, so the label is told it
       may be squeezed and the full name lives in the row's tooltip. Both
       sabotage of that one policy takes the compact row from 14 px to 133 px,
       well past the bound. -->

  <setup project="new"/>

  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>

    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="0"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.test.clap.stereoskew"
                   name="Smaragd Test Stereo Skew" vendor="Smaragd"
                   path="twtestclap.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>

    <!-- ========== 1. THE COMPACT ROW'S SHAPE ========================== -->
    <!-- The name is smaller than the row AND set explicitly: on Linux and
         Windows no theme names a dock-title font, so treeFont() equals the
         application font there and a font EQUALITY would pass with the
         setFont() call deleted (QBX-102's own lesson). nameSmaller is the
         requirement; nameFontSet is what makes it non-vacuous. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotCount="1" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="compact=1|nameSmaller=1|nameFontSet=1|bypassBelowName=1"/>
    <!-- ...and the checkmark carries no text of its own. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotIndex="0"
                         absent="bypassText=Bypass"/>
    <!-- It fits a mixer column, which is the whole reason for the stacking. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" maxRowWidth="60"/>
    <!-- Nothing was shown parentless while the compact row was built: the
         stacking adds a layout, not a widget made visible before its parent
         adopts it (QBX-117). -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotCount="1" strayWindows="0"/>

    <!-- THE TRACK DETAIL DOCK KEEPS THE FULL ROW. Same class, the other
         mount: one line, the labelled checkbox beside the name, and the name
         at the row's own font. If compact leaked into the dock this flips. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="0" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="compact=0|nameSmaller=0|nameFontSet=0|bypassBelowName=0|bypassText=Bypass"/>

    <!-- ========== 2. THE MENU ON AN ACTIVE ROW ======================== -->
    <!-- In menu order, `1` enabled, `0` greyed. No `reload` at all: there is
         nothing to re-resolve on an Active slot, and the BUTTON is not built
         there either, so the menu and the row agree. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="menu=edit=1,bypass=1,remove=1"/>
    <!-- `,reload=` and not `reload`: describeSlot's OWN older field says
         whether a Reload BUTTON was built (`reload=0` here), so the bare word
         appears either way. The comma is the menu list's separator, which is
         what makes this an assertion about the menu. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotIndex="0"
                         absent=",reload="/>
    <!-- ...and the same menu in the dock's mount: the commands are the row's,
         not the mixer's. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="0" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="menu=edit=1,bypass=1,remove=1"/>

    <!-- `reload` is REFUSED on an Active row, which is the other half of it
         not being offered. -->
    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" command="reload" expect="0"/>

    <!-- ========== 3. BYPASS FROM THE MENU ITEM ======================== -->
    <!-- The item clicks the row's REAL checkbox, so this goes through
         onPluginBypassToggled() and therefore through set-plugin-bypass
         (pluginui/CONTRACT.md inv. 3). The UNDO is what proves it was an
         action and not a direct slot poke — a poke would leave nothing to
         undo and the count below would fail. -->
    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" command="bypass"/>
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="bypass=1"/>
    <!-- The menu now shows the state it is about, checked. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="menu=edit=1,bypass=1*,remove=1"/>

    <undo count="1"/>
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="bypass=0"/>

    <!-- ========== 4. EDIT FROM THE MENU ITEM ========================== -->
    <!-- The fixture has no clap.gui, so the plugin window for this slot is the
         generic slider list (proposal 33 D3's fallback, gated as a DECISION by
         plugin_ui_strip_and_editor). Nothing is put on screen: in
         test-case mode openParamEditor() builds and attaches the editor without
         showing it, which is what makes the registry readable here. -->
    <assert-plugin-editor-kind trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" expect="generic"/>
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="assert" expectOpen="0"/>

    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" command="edit"/>
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="assert" expectOpen="1"/>
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="close" expectOpen="0"/>

    <!-- ...and the DOUBLE-CLICK on the row does the same thing, as a real
         MouseButtonDblClick delivered to the row's container. Remove the
         installEventFilter() call and this stops opening anything. -->
    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" gesture="double-click"/>
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="assert" expectOpen="1"/>
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" action="close" expectOpen="0"/>

    <!-- ========== 5. A MISSING ROW'S MENU AND ITS REFUSALS ============ -->
    <insert-plugin trackPath="0" slotIndex="1"
                   format="clap" uid="tw.nobody.ships.this.plugin"
                   name="Nonexistent Reverb" vendor="Acme"
                   path="nosuchmodule.clap" nIn="2" nOut="2"/>

    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotCount="2" slotIndex="1"
                         contains="state=Missing"/>
    <!-- Edit and Bypass are GREYED — the placeholder has no parameters and is
         already transparent — Reload is offered, and Remove is offered in
         every state, because remove-plugin is Missing-tolerant and "I cannot
         remove a plugin even if it is missing" is the complaint CONTRACT
         inv. 8 was filed under. -->
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotIndex="1"
                         contains="menu=edit=0,bypass=0,reload=1,remove=1"/>

    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="1" command="edit" expect="0"/>
    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="1" command="bypass" expect="0"/>
    <!-- Refused, so nothing opened and nothing was bypassed. -->
    <plugin-generic-editor trackIndex="0" slotIndex="1" action="assert" expectOpen="0"/>
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotIndex="1"
                         contains="bypass=0"/>

    <!-- Reload IS offered on a Missing row. It cannot succeed here (nobody
         ships that plugin), and that is the point of the slot staying Missing
         with its stored state chunk untouched — the command being reachable
         is what is claimed, not that it finds anything. -->
    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="1" command="reload" expect="1"/>
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotCount="2" slotIndex="1"
                         contains="name=Nonexistent Reverb (missing)|state=Missing"/>

    <!-- ========== 6. REMOVE FROM THE MENU ITEM ======================== -->
    <!-- The headline: in the mixer's mount this is the ONLY route to it. -->
    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="1" command="remove"/>
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotCount="1" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="state=Active"/>

    <!-- ...through remove-plugin, so it undoes. -->
    <undo count="1"/>
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotCount="2" slotIndex="1"
                         contains="state=Missing"/>

    <!-- And the Active row can be removed too, from the same item. -->
    <plugin-row-command trackIndex="0" slotIndex="0" command="remove"/>
    <assert-plugin-strip trackIndex="0" compact="1" slotCount="1" slotIndex="0"
                         contains="state=Missing"/>
  </actions>

  <assertions>
    <assert-track-count equals="1"/>
  </assertions>

</SActionScript>
